# M3b route (b): virtio-gpu. Guest front-end half only.
#
# The UML arm64 port already carries a native virtio bus driver,
# arch/um/drivers/virtio_uml.c: virtio devices over a vhost-user UNIX
# socket, instantiated from the kernel command line with
#   virtio_uml.device=<socket path>:<virtio device id>
# (device id 16 = VIRTIO_ID_GPU, include/uapi/linux/virtio_ids.h).
# No MMIO plumbing needed on the guest side: the host end is a
# vhost-user device we implement in the console app's native helper,
# not a fake platform device.
#
# Gates checked against this tree:
#   - VIRTIO_UML (arch/um/drivers/Kconfig): select VIRTIO, no deps.
#   - DRM (drivers/gpu/drm/Kconfig:10): depends on (AGP||AGP=n) &&
#     !EMULATED_CMPXCHG && HAS_DMA. UML defaults AGP off and does not select
#     EMULATED_CMPXCHG. HAS_DMA: verified on this tree -- UML_IOMEM_EMULATION
#     alone opens HAS_IOMEM but NOT HAS_DMA (olddefconfig silently dropped
#     DRM); the tree ships a dedicated gate, UML_DMA_EMULATION (arch/um/Kconfig:87,
#     "Provide the DMA API on top of ordinary memory ... Say Y if you need a
#     subsystem that depends on HAS_DMA"). Bookkeeping, no real transfers.
#   - DRM_VIRTIO_GPU: depends on DRM && VIRTIO_MENU && MMU -- all fine;
#     pulls KMS helpers, GEM shmem, VIRTIO_DMA_SHARED_BUFFER.
#
# Phase 1 target = DRM/KMS scanout (frame copy to the app surface).
# virgl/gfxstream (3D) is deliberately NOT here: VIRTIO_GPU_F_VIRGL host
# work is a separate project behind this one, and a broken half of it
# would poison the scanout path. KMS-only first, 3D later.
CONFIG_UML_DMA_EMULATION=y
CONFIG_VIRTIO_UML=y
CONFIG_DRM=y
CONFIG_DRM_VIRTIO_GPU=y
